AB  - The underlying mechanisms of many pain conditions are not known and many conditions have no effective treatment. Modern dynamic neuroimaging have increased the understanding of altered CNS processing in different pain conditions. This chapter describes the use of advanced MR imaging techniques like fMRI, MR spectroscopy, and diffusion-weighted imaging as well as more established techniques like PET and SPECT in pain conditions in general with more focused attention to fibromyalgia. © Springer Science+Business Media, LLC 2011. All rights reserved.
